  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA containing NNN integers.\n\nYou can delete **at most two** of its elements.\n\nFind the minimum possible value of (max⁡(A)−min⁡(A))(\\max(A) - \\min(A))(max(A)−min(A)) (in other words, the range of AAA) after the deletions.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible value of max⁡(A)−min⁡(A)\\max(A) - \\min(A)max(A)−min(A) after at most two deletions.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "3≤N≤2⋅1053 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^53≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n2 3 1\n5\n1 10000 10 100 1000\n6\n64 11 998 1005 843 945",
        "output": "0\n99\n162",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Delete 111 and 222 to make the array A=[3]A = [3]A=[3].\nmax⁡(A)−min⁡(A)=0\\max(A) - \\min(A) = 0max(A)−min(A)=0 which is the best we can do.\nTest case 222: Delete A2=10000A_2 = 10000A2​=10000 and A5=1000A_5 = 1000A5​=1000 to obtain A=[1,10,100]A = [1, 10, 100]A=[1,10,100], for which max⁡(A)−min⁡(A)=99\\max(A) - \\min(A) = 99max(A)−min(A)=99.\nTest case 333: Delete A1=64A_1 = 64A1​=64 and A2=11A_2 = 11A2​=11 to obtain A=[998,1005,843,945]A = [998, 1005, 843, 945]A=[998,1005,843,945], which has a range of 162162162."
      }
    ]
  },
